  "title": "51: al-Zaareyaat الذاريات",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-beneficent, the All-merciful\nوَالذّٰرِيٰتِ ذَرْوًا ۙ‏(1)\n\nBy the scattering [winds] that scatter [the clouds];\nفَالْحٰمِلٰتِ وِقْرًا ۙ‏(2)\n\nby the [rain] bearing [clouds] laden [with water];\nفَالْجٰرِيٰتِ يُسْرًا ۙ‏(3)\n\nby [the ships] which move gently [on the sea];\nفَالْمُقَسِّمٰتِ اَمْرًا ۙ‏(4)\n\nby [the angels] who dispense [livelihood] by [His] command:\nاِنَّمَا تُوْعَدُوْنَ لَصَادِقٌ ۙ‏(5)\n\nindeed what you are promised is true,\nوَّاِنَّ الدِّيْنَ لوَاقِعٌ ؕ‏(6)\n\nand indeed the retribution will surely come to pass!\nوَالسَّمَآءِ ذَاتِ الْحُبُكِ ۙ‏(7)\n\nBy the sky full of adornment [with stars],\nاِنَّكُمْ لَفِىْ قَوْلٍ مُّخْتَلِفٍ ۙ‏(8)\n\nindeed you are of different opinions!\nيُّؤْفَكُ عَنْهُ مَنْ اُفِكَ ؕ‏(9)\n\nHe who has been turned away [from the truth] is turned away from it.\nقُتِلَ الْخَرّٰصُوْنَۙ‏(10)\n\nPerish the liars,\nالَّذِيْنَ هُمْ فِىْ غَمْرَةٍ سَاهُوْنَۙ‏(11)\n\nwho are heedless in a stupor!\nيَسْئَلُوْنَ اَيَّانَ يَوْمُ الدِّيْنِؕ‏(12)\n\nThey ask, ‘When will be the Day of Retribution?’\nيَوْمَ هُمْ عَلَى النَّارِ يُفْتَنُوْنَ‏(13)\n\nIt is the day when they will be tormented in the Fire,\nذُوْقُوْا فِتْنَتَكُمْؕ هٰذَا الَّذِىْ كُنْتُمْ بِهٖ تَسْتَعْجِلُوْنَ‏(14)\n\n[and will be told]: ‘Taste your torment. This is what you used to hasten.’\nاِنَّ الْمُتَّقِيْنَ فِىْ جَنّٰتٍ وَّعُيُوْنٍۙ‏(15)\n\nIndeed the Godwary will be amid gardens and springs,\nاٰخِذِيْنَ مَاۤ اٰتٰٮهُمْ رَبُّهُمْ‌ؕ اِنَّهُمْ كَانُوْا قَبْلَ ذٰلِكَ مُحْسِنِيْنَؕ‏(16)\n\nreceiving what their Lord has given them, for they had been virtuous aforetime.\nكَانُوْا قَلِيْلًا مِّنَ الَّيْلِ مَا يَهْجَعُوْنَ‏(17)\n\nThey used to sleep a little during the night,\nوَبِالْاَسْحَارِ هُمْ يَسْتَغْفِرُوْنَ‏(18)\n\nand at dawns they would plead for forgiveness,\nوَفِىْۤ اَمْوَالِهِمْ حَقٌّ لِّلسَّآئِلِ وَالْمَحْرُوْمِ‏(19)\n\nand there was a share in their wealth for the beggar and the deprived.\nوَفِى الْاَرْضِ اٰيٰتٌ لِّلْمُوْقِنِيْنَۙ‏(20)\n\nIn the earth are signs for those who have conviction,\nوَفِىْۤ اَنْفُسِكُمْ‌ؕ اَفَلَا تُبْصِرُوْنَ‏(21)\n\nand in your souls [as well]. Will you not then perceive?\nوَفِى السَّمَآءِ رِزْقُكُمْ وَمَا تُوْعَدُوْنَ‏(22)\n\nAnd in the sky is your provision and what you are promised.\nفَوَرَبِّ السَّمَآءِ وَالْاَرْضِ اِنَّهٗ لَحَقٌّ مِّثْلَ مَاۤ اَنَّكُمْ تَنْطِقُوْنَ‏(23)\n\nBy the Lord of the sky and the earth, it is indeed the truth, just as [it is a fact that] you speak.\nهَلْ اَتٰٮكَ حَدِيْثُ ضَيْفِ اِبْرٰهِيْمَ الْمُكْرَمِيْنَ‌ۘ‏(24)\n\nDid you receive the story of Abraham’s honoured guests?\nاِذْ دَخَلُوْا عَلَيْهِ فَقَالُوْا سَلٰمًا‌ؕ قَالَ سَلٰمٌ ۚ قَوْمٌ مُّنْكَرُوْنَ‌‏(25)\n\nWhen they entered into his presence, they said, ‘Peace!’ ‘Peace!’ He answered, ‘[You are] an unfamiliar folk.’\nفَرَاغَ اِلٰٓى اَهْلِهٖ فَجَآءَ بِعِجْلٍ سَمِيْنٍۙ‏(26)\n\nThen he retired to his family and brought a fat [roasted] calf,\nفَقَرَّبَهٗۤ اِلَيْهِمْ قَالَ اَلَا تَاْكُلُوْنَ‏(27)\n\nand put it near them. He said, ‘Will you not eat?’\nفَاَوْجَسَ مِنْهُمْ خِيْفَةً‌ؕ قَالُوْا لَا تَخَفْ‌ ؕ وَبَشَّرُوْهُ بِغُلٰمٍ عَلِيْمٍ‏(28)\n\nThen he felt a fear of them. They said, ‘Do not be afraid!’ and they gave him the good news of a wise son.\nفَاَقْبَلَتِ امْرَاَتُهٗ فِىْ صَرَّةٍ فَصَكَّتْ وَجْهَهَا وَقَالَتْ عَجُوْزٌ عَقِيْمٌ‏(29)\n\nThen his wife came forward crying [with joy]. She beat her face, and said, ‘A barren old woman!’\nقَالُوْا كَذٰلِكِ ۙ قَالَ رَبُّكِ‌ؕ اِنَّهٗ هُوَ الْحَكِيْمُ الْعَلِيْمُ‏(30)\n\nThey said, ‘So has your Lord said. Indeed He is the All-wise, the All-knowing.’\nقَالَ فَمَا خَطْبُكُمْ اَيُّهَا الْمُرْسَلُوْنَ‏(31)\n\nHe said, ‘O messengers, what is now your errand?’\nقَالُوْۤا اِنَّاۤ اُرْسِلْنَاۤ اِلٰى قَوْمٍ مُّجْرِمِيْنَۙ‏(32)\n\nThey said, ‘We have been sent toward a guilty people,\nلِنُرْسِلَ عَلَيْهِمْ حِجَارَةً مِّنْ طِيْنٍۙ‏(33)\n\nthat We may rain upon them stones of clay,\nمُّسَوَّمَةً عِنْدَ رَبِّكَ لِلْمُسْرِفِيْنَ‏(34)\n\nsent for the transgressors from your Lord.\nفَاَخْرَجْنَا مَنْ كَانَ فِيْهَا مِنَ الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ‌ۚ‏(35)\n\nSo We picked out those who were in it of the faithful,\nفَمَا وَجَدْنَا فِيْهَا غَيْرَ بَيْتٍ مِّنَ الْمُسْلِمِيْنَ‌ۚ‏(36)\n\nbut We did not find there other than one house of Muslims,\nوَتَرَكْنَا فِيْهَاۤ اٰيَةً لِّلَّذِيْنَ يَخَافُوْنَ الْعَذَابَ الْاَلِيْمَؕ‏(37)\n\nand We have left therein a sign for those who fear a painful punishment.’\nوَفِىْ مُوْسٰۤی اِذْ اَرْسَلْنٰهُ اِلٰى فِرْعَوْنَ بِسُلْطٰنٍ مُّبِيْنٍ‏(38)\n\nAnd in Moses [too there is a sign] when We sent him to Pharaoh with a manifest authority.\nفَتَوَلّٰى بِرُكْنِهٖ وَقَالَ سٰحِرٌ اَوْ مَجْنُوْنٌ‏(39)\n\nBut he turned away assured of his might, and said, ‘A magician or a crazy man!’\nفَاَخَذْنٰهُ وَجُنُوْدَهٗ فَنَبَذْنٰهُمْ فِى الْيَمِّ وَهُوَ مُلِيْمٌؕ‏(40)\n\nSo We seized him and his hosts, and cast them into the sea, while he was blameworthy.\nوَفِىْ عَادٍ اِذْ اَرْسَلْنَا عَلَيْهِمُ الرِّيْحَ الْعَقِيْمَ‌ۚ‏(41)\n\nAnd in ‘Ad when We unleashed upon them a barren wind.\nمَا تَذَرُ مِنْ شَىْءٍ اَتَتْ عَلَيْهِ اِلَّا جَعَلَتْهُ كَالرَّمِيْمِؕ‏(42)\n\nIt left nothing that it came upon without making it like decayed bones.\nوَفِىْ ثَمُوْدَ اِذْ قِيْلَ لَهُمْ تَمَتَّعُوْا حَتّٰى حِيْنٍ‏(43)\n\nAnd in Thamud, when they were told, ‘Enjoy for a while.’\nفَعَتَوْا عَنْ اَمْرِ رَبِّهِمْ فَاَخَذَتْهُمُ الصّٰعِقَةُ وَ هُمْ يَنْظُرُوْنَ‏(44)\n\nThen they defied the command of their Lord; so the thunderbolt seized them as they looked on.\nفَمَا اسْتَطَاعُوْا مِنْ قِيَامٍ وَّمَا كَانُوْا مُنْتَصِرِيْنَۙ‏(45)\n\nSo they were neither able to rise up, nor to come to one another’s aid.\nوَقَوْمَ نُوْحٍ مِّنْ قَبْلُ‌ؕ اِنَّهُمْ كَانُوْا قَوْمًا فٰسِقِيْنَ‏(46)\n\nAnd the people of Noah aforetime. Indeed, they were a transgressing lot.\nوَ السَّمَآءَ بَنَيْنٰهَا بِاَيْٮدٍ وَّاِنَّا لَمُوْسِعُوْنَ‏(47)\n\nWe have built the heaven with might, and indeed it is We who are its expanders.\nوَالْاَرْضَ فَرَشْنٰهَا فَنِعْمَ الْمٰهِدُوْنَ‏(48)\n\nAnd We have spread out the earth, so how excellent spreaders We have been!\nوَمِنْ كُلِّ شَىْءٍ خَلَقْنَا زَوْجَيْنِ لَعَلَّكُمْ تَذَكَّرُوْنَ‏(49)\n\nIn all things We have created pairs so that you may take admonition.\nفَفِرُّوْۤا اِلَى اللّٰهِ‌ؕ اِنِّىْ لَكُمْ مِّنْهُ نَذِيْرٌ مُّبِيْنٌ‌ۚ‏(50)\n\n‘So flee toward Allah. Indeed, I am from Him a manifest warner to you.\nوَلَا تَجْعَلُوْا مَعَ اللّٰهِ اِلٰهًا اٰخَرَ‌ؕ اِنِّىْ لَكُمْ مِّنْهُ نَذِيْرٌ مُّبِيْنٌ‌ۚ‏(51)\n\nDo not set up another god besides Allah. Indeed I am from Him a manifest warner to you.’\nكَذٰلِكَ مَاۤ اَتَى الَّذِيْنَ مِنْ قَبْلِهِمْ مِّنْ رَّسُوْلٍ اِلَّا قَالُوْا سَاحِرٌ اَوْ مَجْنُوْنٌ‌ۚ‏(52)\n\nSo it was that there did not come any apostle to those who were before them but they said, ‘A magician,’ or ‘A crazy man!’\nاَتَوَاصَوْا بِهٖ‌ۚ بَلْ هُمْ قَوْمٌ طَاغُوْنَ‌ۚ‏(53)\n\nDid they enjoin this upon one another?! Rather, they were a rebellious lot.\nفَتَوَلَّ عَنْهُمْ فَمَاۤ اَنْتَ بِمَلُوْمٍ‏(54)\n\nSo turn away from them, as you will not be blameworthy.\nوَّذَكِّرْ فَاِنَّ الذِّكْرٰى تَنْفَعُ الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ‏(55)\n\nAnd admonish, for admonition indeed benefits the faithful.\nوَمَا خَلَقْتُ الْجِنَّ وَالْاِنْسَ اِلَّا لِيَعْبُدُوْنِ‏(56)\n\nI did not create the jinn and the humans except that they may worship Me.\nمَاۤ اُرِيْدُ مِنْهُمْ مِّنْ رِّزْقٍ وَّمَاۤ اُرِيْدُ اَنْ يُّطْعِمُوْنِ‏(57)\n\nI desire no provision from them, nor do I desire that they should feed Me.\nاِنَّ اللّٰهَ هُوَ الرَّزَّاقُ ذُو الْقُوَّةِ الْمَتِيْنُ‏(58)\n\nIndeed it is Allah who is the All-provider, Powerful and All-strong.\nفَاِنَّ لِلَّذِيْنَ ظَلَمُوْا ذَنُوْبًا مِّثْلَ ذَنُوْبِ اَصْحٰبِهِمْ فَلَا يَسْتَعْجِلُوْنِ‏(59)\n\nIndeed the lot of those who do wrong [now] will be like the lot of their [earlier] counterparts. So let them not ask Me to hasten on [that fate].\nفَوَيْلٌ لِّلَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا مِنْ يَّوْمِهِمُ الَّذِىْ يُوْعَدُوْنَ‏(60)\n\nWoe to the faithless for the day they are promised!",
  "merits": "Surah al-Zaareyaat (The Scatterers)\nThere are 60 verses in this Surah and it was revealed in Makkah. In the commentary of Majma’ul Bayan it is narrated from the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) that the reward for reciting this Surah is ten times the number of moving winds or breezes.\nImam Ja’far al-Sadiq (a.s.) has said that recitation of this Surah increases ones sustenance and makes it easy to earn. Drinking water in which this Surah was dissolved after being written acts as a remedy for back problems (e.g. backaches). If a pregnant woman wears a talisman of Surah al-Zaareyaat, her pregnancy and delivery will be easy. Keeping this Surah close to a dying person makes his death easy."
}
